From 3ff686719d652da3c298f45144c83123d33224b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clifford Swartz <cliffordswartz1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:13:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] hw/adc: PIC32CM JH/MC ADC (U2247)

Conversions completed at once on SWTRIG.START, on enable and each
RESULT read in free-running mode: AIN0-11 from the board ("ain", the
same interface as the SAM D5x ADC, so the web bench's pots reach it),
INTREF 1.0 V, VDDCORE/4, VDDANA/4; references INTREF, INTVCC0 =
VDDANA/1.48 (the MC00 data sheet's ADC characteristics; the DFP header
says 1/1.6, silicon to decide), INTVCC1 = VDDANA/2, INTVCC2 = VDDANA,
VREFA ("vrefa"); 8/10/12-bit and 16-bit averaging, differential mode
against an AIN or GND, offset/gain correction, LEFTADJ, the window
monitor, RESRDY/OVERRUN/WINMON on one IRQ line. Regenerated tables with
the new adc_u2247 overlay (hooks on CTRLA, CTRLC, SWTRIG, RESULT).

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted; not for submission to upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
